          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The highest common factor of two numbers is 5. The lowest common multiple is 150.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-q16-stem-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 0,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What could the two numbers be? Is there more than one answer?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, 5 and 150, or 25 and 30. Yes, there is more than one answer.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{LCM}&=\\frac{\\text{product}}{\\text{HCF}}\\\\150&=\\frac{\\text{product}}{5}\\\\\\text{product}&=150\\times5=750\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth numbers must be multiples of $5$. Two possible pairs with product $750$ are $(5,150)$ and $(25,30)$.\n\nFor $5$ and $150$, the HCF is $5$ and the LCM is $150$.\n\nFor $25$ and $30$, the HCF is $5$ and the LCM is $25\\times30\\div5=150$.\n\nYes, there is more than one answer.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
